      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 3–5 at.% Sn during melting will improve the oxygen resistance of equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6981790::web::002::1_introduction",
        "PMC7040784::web::010::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sn addition will promote a continuous, adherent, Sn-enriched surface oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Sn-enriched oxide scale will act as a barrier to oxygen diffusion and retard oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sn acts as a reactive element that preferentially oxidizes at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sn can suppress pest oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7040784::web::010::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 3–5 at.% Sn addition will preserve the beneficial single-phase BCC microstructure of equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "mechanism; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The single-phase BCC microstructure is responsible for the alloy's balanced mechanical properties.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Sn-modified alloy will show significantly less pest oxidation than the undoped alloy after 5 hours in air at 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7040784::web::010::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Sn-modified alloy will retain room-temperature tensile ductility in the range of 8–16%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Sn-modified alloy will retain high-temperature yield strength in the range of 163–530 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping Sn at a low concentration can avoid formation of an A15-Nb3Sn-type secondary phase.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6981790::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxidation benefit applies to as-cast samples in air at 800–1000 °C for up to about 5 hours.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sn can affect macrosegregation, reduce liquidus temperature, and affect the stability of the Nb solid solution in Nb-silicide-based alloys.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
